  "tests": {
    "$comment": "Each backend/tests/test_*.py and the contexts it exercises, read by scripts/affected_tests.py to run only the tests a change can break, and checked by scripts/check_architecture.py: a test file in neither 'files' nor 'always', an unknown context, a rule naming no test, or an entry for a file that does not exist fails. A test's contexts are the top of what it imports and of the routes it calls (a router stands for the contexts it imports): a test of loop runs whenever loop or a context loop may import changes, so a context another of a test's contexts may import is left out as implied. 'repo' marks a test that reads repository files (scripts, workflows, docs, the frontend) rather than the backend's modules: it runs when a file it names changes ('mentions' in sources) or when it changes. A new test's entry starts from `python3 scripts/affected_tests.py --suggest backend/tests/<file>` and is read by hand.",
    "sources": {
      "$comment": "How a changed file outside backend/app/services/<context>/ and backend/tests/ is read, by its longest prefix: a context (the tests of that context and of every context that may import it), 'imports' (the contexts the module imports, platform when none: the routers and the app's own modules), 'mentions' (the tests whose text names the file's path, its name or one of its folders two levels deep or more), 'all' (the whole suite) or a test file by name. A path no prefix matches runs the whole suite.",
